From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dfs: restore operating channel width when no channel is found

dfs_downgrade_bandwidth() walks the configured operating width down
(160 -> 80 -> 40/20) via hostapd_set_oper_chwidth() while it searches for
a usable channel. When every candidate is in NOP it gives up and returns
NULL, but the mutated width is left behind in iface->conf. The center
segment index (seg0) is only written back on the success paths, so it
still describes the original, wider channel.

On a 160 MHz DFS channel a single radar event NOPs all eight 20 MHz
sub-channels at once, so the search always fails. hostapd then toggles the
interface into DFS state (hostapd_disable_iface()/hostapd_enable_iface()).
When the NOP expires hostapd_dfs_nop_finished() calls hostapd_handle_dfs(),
which restarts CAC using the mutated width together with the untouched
seg0:

  DFS-CAC-START freq=5640 chan=128 sec_chan=-1, width=0, seg0=114, ...

hostapd_set_freq_params() rejects that combination in its
CONF_OPER_CHWIDTH_USE_HT case ("center segment 0 and center freq 1 not in
sync"), hostapd_start_dfs_cac() returns -1, and hostapd_handle_dfs() logs
"DFS start_dfs_cac() failed, -1". That return value is discarded by
hostapd_dfs_nop_finished(), so nothing retries and the radio stays in
HAPD_IFACE_DFS state indefinitely.

This is a generic upstream hostapd bug (the width leak in
dfs_downgrade_bandwidth() combined with the now-upstream "enter DFS state
if no available channel is found" toggle); it has been reported against
ath10k, ath11k and mt76 on OpenWrt (issues #13231, #14253, #19371) with
no fix proposed. Restore the saved operating width on both failure paths
so the CAC retried after the NOP uses a chandef consistent with the
configured center segment and recovers on its own.

Signed-off-by: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
--- a/src/ap/dfs.c
+++ b/src/ap/dfs.c
@@ -1336,6 +1336,7 @@
 	enum dfs_channel_type channel_type = DFS_ANY_CHANNEL;
 	int err = 1;
 	u8 op_class, chan;
+	u8 current_vht_oper_chwidth = hostapd_get_oper_chwidth(iface->conf);
 
 	/* Radar detected during active CAC */
 	iface->cac_started = 0;
@@ -1350,6 +1351,16 @@
 						  &oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx,
 						  &channel_type);
 		if (!channel) {
+			/*
+			 * dfs_downgrade_bandwidth() walked the operating
+			 * width down while searching and left the reduced
+			 * value in iface->conf even though no channel was
+			 * found. Restore it so a later CAC attempt is not
+			 * built with a width that no longer matches the
+			 * configured center segment.
+			 */
+			hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf,
+						 current_vht_oper_chwidth);
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "No valid channel available");
 			return err;
 		}
@@ -1477,6 +1488,17 @@
 						  &channel_type);
 		if (!channel) {
 			/*
+			 * dfs_downgrade_bandwidth() mutates the configured
+			 * operating width as it searches. When it finds
+			 * nothing the reduced width stays in iface->conf
+			 * while the center segment index does not, so the
+			 * CAC restarted from hostapd_dfs_nop_finished()
+			 * would build an inconsistent chandef and fail in
+			 * hostapd_set_freq_params(). Restore the width.
+			 */
+			hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf,
+						 current_vht_oper_chwidth);
+			/*
 			 * Toggle interface state to enter DFS state
 			 * until NOP is finished.
 			 */
